## Production Polish Sprint — April 2, 2026

Six pre-launch complaints solved before they happened. Audit-driven session.

### What shipped

**Pipedream Connect OAuth (replaces all custom OAuth)**
All channel connections now use Pipedream managed auth. The entire OAuth layer — redirect URIs, developer app approvals, token refresh, sensitive scope review — is handled by Pipedream. Implementation: single `connect.html` iframe built directly with token in query params + postMessage listener. No SDK dependency needed.

Channels on Pipedream Connect: LinkedIn, Facebook, Reddit, HubSpot, Webflow.
Channels staying manual: X/Twitter (X asked Pipedream to remove it), Ghost (key-based), WordPress (app password), Medium (legacy).

Key learning: bypassing the Pipedream SDK entirely and building the iframe directly was the correct call. The SDK's token resolution was broken across multiple attempts. The iframe URL `pipedream.com/_static/connect.html?token=xxx&app=slug` is the ground truth.

**Content Library (`/app/content-library`)**
Every article ever generated, across all brands, in one searchable view. Card grid with hero images, confidence scores, status chips, publish channels, performance stats. Search debounced 350ms. Status tabs (All/Published/Staged/Draft) with live counts. Preview modal with live post links and Go to Queue. Brand filter is top-level in the header — clearly marked as agency/internal, can be removed for single-brand production with one CSS change.

**Inline Article Editing**
Content preview modal in Publishing Queue now supports click-to-edit on every text element: title, meta description, section headings, section body. Edits save to DB on blur via `PATCH /api/content/:brandSafeId/:contentId`. Title edits also sync to the queue item. No round-trip through Compliance Gate for small copy changes. The edit hint `✎` appears on hover — discoverable without being noisy.

**External Review Workflow (`/review/[token]`)**
"Send for Review" share icon on every queue card. Generates a signed 48-char hex token, stores against the queue item, copies link to clipboard. Reviewer opens URL — no login, no account. Full article renders (hero, title, body, meta). Sticky review panel: comment textarea + Approve (green) + Request Changes (amber). On action, status writes back to `publishing_queue`. Queue card shows review badge: ✓ Approved (green), ↩ Changes Requested (amber), ⏳ Pending (grey) + inline comment preview. First test: approved with comment "Slay". ✅

**Queue Card Inline Title Edit**
Click any article title on a queue card → editable input. Enter or blur saves via `PATCH /api/publishing/queue/:id/title`. Edit pencil hint on hover.

**Live Article Preview Link**
External link icon on queue cards → `/articles/:brandSlug/:articleSlug` in new tab. Brand slug resolved via server-side join on `brand_profiles` in queue query.

